      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We evaluated residents regarding maintenance treatment of asthma and the technique for using metered dose inhalers. Methods. Residents were asked to prescribe a treatment for a patient with poorly controlled persistent asthma and to demonstrate the use of metered dose inhaler (MDI) medication. Results. 76% of 239 residents correctly identified the medication indicated for the case; only 30% of them adequately performed the inhalation technique (49% from HCFMUSP vs. 19% from other institutions; p < 0.001). Conclusions. The results demonstrate that, when seeing a typical patient with uncontrolled persistent asthma, most residents are able to correctly identify the drugs indicated for treatment but not adequately instruct the MDI technique use."},
